  it said you only have to accept healthy  love  on my headboard on the back of my front  door  was a post-it note that says you are  ready for the world  and the world is ready for you that was  1997.  like that's how important those  affirmations were in getting me back  up and getting me back into my power  turning my crawl into a walk in my walk  into a run in my run into a sore  and so if you want to get back in your  power begin to read things and write  things to remind you  of who you've always been you may not  see the evidence now  but it doesn't mean it isn't so second  thing  is to get people that can remind you of  who you've been  get people to pour into your ears pour  into your mind pour into your soul  i remember i was on stage once and this  woman yelled out at the end of my speech  you're an amazing mom  and this particular day i didn't feel  amazing at all i had been on the road  for 11 days and i left jelani with my  mom and i had never been  away from him for 11 days i felt  horrible  and so i felt like i was a fraud so i  walked off stage and i called a good  friend of mine  who's always with jelani and i and i  said can you please tell me  why you think that i'm a great mom  because she had told me that i was a  great mom many times  i said can you tell me why you say that  what do you see  and for the next 15 minutes she was like  i was like i need evidence  she just gave me evidence of what made  me a great mom in her  eyes sometimes you need to look at  yourself through someone else's lenses  because their lens of you is cleaner  than your lens of yourself  the third thing i want to remind you is  how do you live in your power  once you've gotten it and and while  you're in it how do you  live in it i'm going to be honest with  you because i'm your sister i'm not here  to just give you rah-rah hoopla  there are some days when while you're  living in your power  it feels as if you're getting further  and further away from it  and on those days remind yourself  and when i say power i don't mean a  dominant power i don't mean a power that  dominates others  i don't mean an egocentric power i mean  a power that keeps you in peace  a power that says i am in the driver's  seat of my life  i'm not a victim of my life every now  and then it feels like things like covet  or things like you know social injustice  or things  that are just happening around you  unexpected death of  of a loved one it feels like it throws  you over into the passenger seat  and it throws you into the back seat and  at times  it throws you in the trunk it's your  birthright  to climb out of the trunk climb out of  the back seat slide over from the  passenger seat  and get back into the driver's seat and  say this is my life  i have one thing that i run from  beginning to end and that's  my life and then just like how you get  back in your power the way you stay  is you get people in your tribe that are  cheerleaders  you get high conscious thinkers don't  get low conscious thinkers  low conscious thinkers will always want  you to keep them company  happiness is one of those conversations  that and experiences that can be a bit  elusive  because people believe that when they  found happiness  that it should stay forever and the  reality is  happiness is one of those ebb and flows  that happiness today  will look differently than happiness did  three years ago  happiness three years from now will look  different  than the way happiness looks for you  today happiness  is something that expands and contracts  happiness  is something that you bring into a room  not what you search for a room to give  to you  what i love about happiness is that it's  something that you can carry with you  it's like a light you know we have  people in our lives and  and you may be one or you may know of  someone where you step into a space  and you measure the joy in the room or  the light  in the room and then you adjust your  light accordingly  happiness is sort of like that light  then there are others  like i've learned to be where you step  into a room  and when you step into a room you  actually bring  the light in the room not that the room  wasn't bright before  you came but you carry your own palette  you carry your own storage  of happiness meaning your temperament of  joy  is set and decided before you  interact or engage with anyone  i'd love to share with you some of the  tools that i've used  to find my happiness that's one journey  to keep my happiness that's another  journey  and to get back to my happiness lord  knows  that's yet another journey so some of  the things that helps  with happiness number one  it's understanding the myth about  happiness someone else  cannot make you happy solely and  exclusively  they can add to your joy but it's no one  else's responsibility  to make you happy than yours when i  realized that when i realized that in  a parent-child relationship my parents  weren't responsible for my happiness  when i realized in a romantic  relationship my partner  wasn't responsible for my happiness that  i  lisa nichols i'm responsible for my  happiness  and everyone around me they add to it  in some cases they might challenge it  but  ultimately happiness my happiness your  happiness  is your responsibility so when you look  at  the journey to happiness or the journey  back to happiness  is there accountability meaning is there  someone in your life  holding you responsible for the person  that you say you want to be  is there someone in your life holding  you as the woman responsible for the  woman you wish to become  for the man you which you wish to show  up as accountability is  powerful in the space of happiness  because then you always have someone  reminding you  of your declaration to yourself  and then to the people who come across  your path  second is authenticity  when i realized how much authenticity  and living  in my truth had to do with my happiness  and i mean  the happiness that's in the dark of the  night when no one's looking  that not that happiness in the middle of  the day that yeah i'm happy  you know that happy that looks more like  this yeah  i'm happy how how about you whereas  people are saying they're happy but on  the inside it's like you're a ticking  bomb  it's like you're holding your breath  it's like the smile  on your face is for everyone else  and it's not for you it's that happy  that says i don't trust you to be able  to handle my truth  that in this moment i'm not i'm not as  happy as i normally am  it's that authenticity that leads to you  being able to say what you need to say  and do what you need to do  to be the man the woman you've always  known yourself to be  it's in not dimming your light because  you're worried that someone can't  handle your light it's in showing up  and standing as tall as you would stand  if no one were looking  standing on your tippy toes allowing  your greatness to enter the room  it's speaking life and to the person  you're becoming  it's also owning your shadow owning that  dark part of you that you  look back at and say i sure wish you  weren't there but since you're there i'm  going to deal with you  authentically happiness  lives inside of authenticity  and the third is can you be honest with  those around you  it lives in the same space as  authenticity but the honesty i'm  speaking of is the willingness to share  with people  who they need you to share with them  it's the willingness to tell people who  you see  it's the willingness to hold others to  their greatness  it's the willingness to remind others  when they're not playing as tall as big  as they can  and as they want to be remembered as  honesty  it's drawing a healthy line in the sand  it's recognizing that if someone keeps  crossing your line  it might not be because they're rude or  disrespectful  it may be because your line isn't deep  enough  it's not bold enough and can you be  honest enough to say hold on  i've trained you to believe that i can  handle everything  and that i don't need acknowledgement  and that i don't need to hear the word  thank you but hold on  i'm learning something from my coach i  really do need to hear thank you  i really do need a timeout periodically  i really do need my me time  it's being willing to be honest with  those around you  about how life feels in their presence  honest enough to say i love you  i need you i apologize  i got caught up in my ego if you want  some amazing affirmations with brendan  burchard check  out the video right there next to me i  think you'll enjoy it continue to  believe  and i'll see you there you really love  marie and you want to do a good job for  her and her people  and this is a book you worked on for  three years and it's important it does  well  and brendan don't forget you're so lucky  you get to do this brother
 

